    {
      "id": "e12499fb-4673-47ab-ac91-cdf0e1b9ecc4",
      "unit_id": "50941d8d-5a5a-4dd4-9d91-f7d6b454ff9a",
      "type": "listening",
      "title": "Giving Personal Information",
      "content": "<p>A: Good morning. Welcome to the City Library. How can I help you? </p><p>B: Good morning. I'd like to become a member, please. </p><p>A: Of course. I just need to take some details. What's your full name? </p><p>B: It's Ethan Fernsby. </p><p>A: Can you spell your first name, please? </p><p>B: Yes. It's E, T, H, A, N. And your last name? F, E, R, N, S, P. Thank you. </p><p>A: And what's your date of birth? </p><p>B: It's the 27th of August, 1986. </p><p>A: Great. What's your address? </p><p>B: I live at 48 Chesterton Avenue, Birmingham. </p><p>A: Could you spell the street name for me? </p><p>B: Sure. C H E S T E R T O, N. And your phone number? It's 078-543-9176. </p><p>A: Sorry, could you repeat that? </p><p>B: Sure. 078-54-329176. </p><p>A: Thanks. Finally. What's your email address? </p><p>B: It's <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://e.fernsby86mail.com\">e.fernsby86mail.com</a>. </p><p>A: Could you spell that for me? </p><p>B: Yes. E, F, E, R, ns b <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://y86mail.com\">y86mail.com</a>. </p><p>A: Got it. You are now registered. Here is your library card. </p><p>B: Thank you very much. How many books can I borrow at the same time? </p><p>A: You can borrow up to three books at once. </p><p>B: And how long can I keep them for? </p><p>A: You have to bring the books back in three weeks. But you can renew them online if needed. </p><p>B: I see. Is there free Wi Fi in the library? </p><p>A: Yes, we offer free Wi Fi. </p><p>B: What's the password? </p><p>A: The password is lib 2459 vis. </p><p>B: Sorry, could you repeat that? </p><p>A: Of course. It's lib 2459 vis. It's written on the notice board near the entrance. </p><p>B: Thanks. Also, where can I find mystery novels? </p><p>A: The mystery section is on the second floor near the window area. </p><p>B: Great. I'll go check it out. </p><p>A: Enjoy your visit and welcome to the library. </p><p></p>",
